{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "006P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-abelian-presheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b06414be3553a9d603dde3d3d1eec69a633fd515107faaba6ad926b8b6791c2f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:99365745b74503e2a765c503254e5eff801dfadc168ed269982bfebb56b3228e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0002>.\nWe would like to define the notion of a presheaf of\n<MATH_0003>-modules over <MATH_0004>. In analogy with Definition\n<REF_0001> we are tempted to define\nthis as a presheaf of sets <MATH_0005> such that for every open\n<MATH_0006> the set <MATH_0007> is endowed with the structure\nof an <MATH_0008>-module compatible with restriction mappings\n(of <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>). However, it is customary\n(and equivalent) to define it as in the following definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed3e26af5a2945ba2398dd74e0705f7fbb480753a97ee2edc0c3e7c2df0fbe9c", "unit_id": "tag:006P:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "006P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\mathcal{O} \\times \\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}(U) \\times \\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}(U)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{O} \\times \\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_{\\text{id} \\times \\varphi} &\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[d]^{\\varphi} \\\\\n\\mathcal{O} \\times \\mathcal{G} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{G}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\Hom_\\mathcal{O}(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-presheaf-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fbc37b4c5bd2d53f8dd9a286adb3584453aaf5e4cf3d65d2c2c8b0be9cb9b376", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:584b104cabceb354bbe687da430177dab4df17ede75e54a44a380cd78ec0e8fa", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space, and let <MATH_0002> be\na presheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>presheaf of <MATH_0004>-modules<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis given by an abelian presheaf <MATH_0005> together with a\nmap of presheaves of sets\n<MATH_0006>\nsuch that for every open <MATH_0007> the map\n<MATH_0008>\ndefines the structure of an <MATH_0009>-module\nstructure on the abelian group <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism <MATH_0011>\nof presheaves of <MATH_0012>-modules<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is a morphism of abelian presheaves\n<MATH_0013> such that\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0014>\ncommutes.\n<STRUCT_0004> The set of <MATH_0015>-module morphisms as above is\ndenoted <MATH_0016>.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category of presheaves of <MATH_0017>-modules\nis denoted <MATH_0018>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc8ef05ba7c20ec7b75b2d23038a5c8915f0293ebcf30813dc10b69a0931d1d6", "unit_id": "tag:006Q:statement"}
